cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use these data or this code, please cite the article and the archived dataset."
title: "quito-digital-foodscape: data, code and interactive maps for 'Findability before visibility'"
type: dataset
version: 1.1.0
date-released: 2026-10-26
license: CC-BY-4.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/Jijadan/quito-digital-foodscape"
url: "https://jijadan.github.io/quito-digital-foodscape/"
abstract: >-
  Register-based census of 420 food establishments in the Historic Centre of
  Quito (Ecuador), with their presence and accumulated recognition on Google
  Maps, Instagram and TikTok (June 2026); the Python analysis pipeline; the
  bilingual interactive maps; and the data and code added in the first round
  of peer review (online verification of the establishments without platform
  presence, anonymized independent coding of the culinary typology and
  sensitivity analyses).
keywords:
  - findability
  - digital stratification
  - food heritage
  - digital food environments
  - spatial analysis
  - Quito
